issue_context.body:
**Describe the problem**

In https://github.com/elixir-ecto/ecto_sql/issues/473#issuecomment-1562068139 it was found that CRDB differs from the PostgreSQL wire protocol implementation. If a transaction enters into the aborted state while in the extended protocol, then all further messages should be ignored until the client sends a Sync message.

CockroachDB does ignore a simple query while in this state, but it incorrectly sends back a ReadyForQuery message to the client. This confuses some drivers.

See https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/protocol-flow.html

**To Reproduce**

This pgwire test reproduces the problem
```
send
Query {"String": "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS t;"}
Query {"String": "CREATE TABLE t (i INT PRIMARY KEY, j INT UNIQUE);"}
Query {"String": "BEGIN"}
----

until ignore=NoticeResponse
ReadyForQuery
ReadyForQuery
ReadyForQuery
----
{"Type":"CommandComplete","CommandTag":"DROP TABLE"}
{"Type":"ReadyForQuery","TxStatus":"I"}
{"Type":"CommandComplete","CommandTag":"CREATE TABLE"}
{"Type":"ReadyForQuery","TxStatus":"I"}
{"Type":"CommandComplete","CommandTag":"BEGIN"}
{"Type":"ReadyForQuery","TxStatus":"T"}


send
Query {"String": "SAVEPOINT s"}
Parse {"Name": "s1", "Query": "INSERT INTO t VALUES ($1, $2)"}
Bind {"PreparedStatement": "s1", "Parameters": [{"text": "1"}, {"text": "2"}]}
Execute
Query {"String": "RELEASE SAVEPOINT s"}
----

until
ReadyForQuery
ReadyForQuery
----
{"Type":"CommandComplete","CommandTag":"SAVEPOINT"}
{"Type":"ReadyForQuery","TxStatus":"T"}
{"Type":"ParseComplete"}
{"Type":"BindComplete"}
{"Type":"CommandComplete","CommandTag":"INSERT 0 1"}
{"Type":"CommandComplete","CommandTag":"RELEASE"}
{"Type":"ReadyForQuery","TxStatus":"T"}

send
Query {"String": "SAVEPOINT s"}
Bind {"PreparedStatement": "s1", "Parameters": [{"text": "2"}, {"text": "2"}]}
Execute
Query {"String": "RELEASE SAVEPOINT s"}
----

# The RELEASE SAVEPOINT command should be ignored and should not return ReadyForQuery.
until
ReadyForQuery
ErrorResponse
----
{"Type":"CommandComplete","CommandTag":"SAVEPOINT"}
{"Type":"ReadyForQuery","TxStatus":"T"}
{"Type":"BindComplete"}
{"Type":"ErrorResponse","Code":"23505","ConstraintName":"t_j_key"}

send
Sync
Query {"String": "ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT s; RELEASE SAVEPOINT s"}
Query {"String": "ROLLBACK"}
----

until
ReadyForQuery
ReadyForQuery
ReadyForQuery
----
{"Type":"ReadyForQuery","TxStatus":"E"}
{"Type":"CommandComplete","CommandTag":"ROLLBACK"}
{"Type":"CommandComplete","CommandTag":"RELEASE"}
{"Type":"ReadyForQuery","TxStatus":"T"}
{"Type":"CommandComplete","CommandTag":"ROLLBACK"}
{"Type":"ReadyForQuery","TxStatus":"I"}
```

**Expected behavior**
The test should pass. (It can be added to **pkg/sql/pgwire/testdata/pgtest/aborted_txn**.)


Jira issue: CRDB-28264

Epic CRDB-27601

comments:
Hm there seems to more nuance to the PostgreSQL implementation of the protocol. This is another test that passes against PG.

```
send
Query {"String": "BEGIN"}
Parse {"Name": "stmt_a", "Query": "INSERT INTO t VALUES ($1, $2)"}
Bind {"PreparedStatement": "stmt_a", "Parameters": [{"text": "2"}, {"text": "2"}]}
Query {"String": "SELECT 1/0"}
Query {"String": "SELECT 2"}
Query {"String": "ROLLBACK"}
Sync
----

until
ReadyForQuery
ErrorResponse
ReadyForQuery
ErrorResponse
ReadyForQuery
ReadyForQuery
ReadyForQuery
----
{"Type":"CommandComplete","CommandTag":"BEGIN"}
{"Type":"ReadyForQuery","TxStatus":"T"}
{"Type":"ParseComplete"}
{"Type":"BindComplete"}
{"Type":"ErrorResponse","Code":"22012"}
{"Type":"ReadyForQuery","TxStatus":"E"}
{"Type":"ErrorResponse","Code":"25P02"}
{"Type":"ReadyForQuery","TxStatus":"E"}
{"Type":"CommandComplete","CommandTag":"ROLLBACK"}
{"Type":"ReadyForQuery","TxStatus":"I"}
{"Type":"ReadyForQuery","TxStatus":"I"}
```

But I would have expected PG to ignore the queries sent after `SELECT 1/0`, since I thought those would be treated as "messages received during the extended protocol after an error."
